sequenceDiagram
    participant CS as Charging Station (Test System)
    participant CSMS as CSMS (System under Test)

    Note over CS,CSMS: Prerequisite(s): n/a
    Note over CS,CSMS: Configuration State: N/a
    Note over CS,CSMS: Memory State: N/a
    Note over CS,CSMS: Reusable State: N/a

    CSMS->>CS: SetChargingProfileRequest (chargingProfile.chargingSchedule.chargingSchedulePeriod.limit = 8.0 or 8000.0)
    Note over CSMS: Validation (Step 1):<br>chargingSchedulePeriod.startPeriod = 0 AND<br>chargingSchedulePeriod.limit = 8.0 (A) or 8000.0 (W)<br>The chargingSchedule contains only one chargingSchedulePeriod
    CS-->>CSMS: SetChargingProfileResponse (status = Accepted)

    CSMS->>CS: SetChargingProfileRequest (chargingProfile.chargingSchedule.chargingSchedulePeriod.limit = 6.0 or 6000.0)
    Note over CSMS: Validation (Step 3):<br>chargingSchedulePeriod.startPeriod = 0 AND<br>chargingSchedulePeriod.limit = 6.0 (A) or 6000.0 (W)<br>The chargingSchedule contains only one chargingSchedulePeriod
    Note over CSMS: Validation (Step 1/3):<br>chargingProfile.id = same id for both chargingProfiles<br>chargingProfile.chargingSchedule.startSchedule must NOT be omitted<br>chargingProfile.stackLevel = configured stackLevel AND<br>chargingProfile.chargingProfilePurpose = equal value for both profiles AND (TxDefaultProfile OR ChargingStationMaxProfile)<br>chargingProfile.chargingProfileKind = equal value for both profiles AND<br>If chargingProfilePurpose is TxDefaultProfile then chargingProfileKind must be Absolute OR Recurring<br>If chargingProfilePurpose is ChargingStationMaxProfile then chargingProfileKind must be Absolute<br>If chargingProfileKind is Recurring then recurrencyKind must NOT be omitted, else omitted<br>The received Charging Profiles must comply with the requirements defined at part 2 specification
    CS-->>CSMS: SetChargingProfileResponse (status = Accepted)

    Note over CS,CSMS: Post scenario validations: N/a
